# Emails

::summary
The Email two-plane surface in the shell wrapper (08-15): the hub-group row IMMEDIATELY after Posts (`icon=mail action=openEmail`), tab=main. Title row = "Email" · thread count · the ACCOUNT CHIP (All accounts ⇄ one connected address, `switchEmailAccount`) · the UNREAD toggle · Compose. A folder segmented-control (Inbox / Priority / Leads / Starred / Sent / Drafts / Archive / All mail / Spam / Trash — a real `?folder=` route each; All = the producer's own Inbox+Archived slice), then the zero-JS SEARCH `::form` (`method=get`, field `q` — WP5; the live builder SPLICES the current account/folder/label/unread narrowing in as hidden inputs so a submit keeps the slice), lead the `split-pane`: LEFT = the thread list (paged `?page=`, Newer / Older rows at the foot), merged across EVERY connected account by date and grouped into four TIER heads in producer order — **Priority** (goldlist gold senders), **Leads** (round-3 classifier), **Everything else**, **Low priority** (round-3 bulk demotion; spam + blocklisted senders never appear) — rows carrying `action=openEmailThread`, `unread=true` = right-side dot, the paperclip = the `clipboard` leading glyph + "n attachments" meta (surf-icons has no paperclip); RIGHT = the reading pane: subject header + Archive/Trash, the triage / goldlist / image-toggle forms and the Refresh row (see "Reading pane writes" below), per-message SSR'd header rows (From `Name <address>` · ABSOLUTE time, the shared `absolute_date` spelling / To · via account), attachment chips linking the download proxy, and the sanitized body as a generic `::embed` iframe (`/email/{thread}/body`, its own sandboxed policy, `cid:` inline images resolved to the attachment proxy — WP6b). Designed empty states: no account → "No email connected — Connect an account" (links `/settings/plugins/mailhost/connect`), no threads, no thread selected. Round 4 + WP6b: compose / reply / drafts ride `/email/compose`, `/send`, `/draft`, `/surfy`, `/drafts/{thread}`, `/discard` behind the send gate. Parity round (08-18): the list foot carries the user-LABEL rail (the classic catalog's names as `?label=` links) and the Email settings link (`/email/settings` — accounts + Make-active switch, remote-images pref, goldlist and blocked-senders panels with zero-field Remove/Unblock forms); row meta carries the classic `(n)` message-count badge and the producer-counted `n attachments`; opening a thread re-runs the classic Stage-A lead re-check; with OAuth unconfigured the no-account state is the classic MAILHOST_NOT_CONFIGURED notice. The product label is Email; only provider strings say Mailhost.
::

